# InForce golden question set (M4). One JSON object per line; # comments and blank lines ignored.
#
# Load and validate with:
#     python -m inforce.cli questions --file questions/golden.jsonl
#
# Fields:
#   qid              stable slug, e.g. "sfb-car-01"
#   text             the question, as a user would ask it. Do NOT quote the
#                    source text — that leaks the answer into retrieval.
#   topic            free text, e.g. "capital adequacy"
#   category         entity category, e.g. "Small Finance Banks"
#   answerable       true (default) or false. Aim for ~10 unanswerable.
#   expected_doc_key the IN-FORCE document that should answer it. Required when
#                    answerable. Validation rejects a withdrawn expected source.
#   expected_quote   the supporting span, pasted from the document. This is what
#                    makes the answer verifiable rather than remembered.
#   trap_doc_keys    WITHDRAWN documents that plausibly answer the same question.
#                    Required — a question no withdrawn document could answer
#                    cannot expose a temporal failure, so it measures nothing.
#   difficulty       easy | medium | hard
#   notes            anything a reviewer needs to know
#
# Find candidate topic pairs with:
#     python -m inforce.cli candidates --top 40
#
# Target: 50-60 answerable + ~10 unanswerable. Budget real time for this — it is
# the gate on N and the step most likely to be rushed.
#
# Example (delete once you have real ones):
